From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:01:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 086/138] ASoC: apple: mca-t7000: Add PIO capture, a codec DAI
 and MCLK pad clocks

Capture works like playback: the RX shim at +0x1800 fills from the MCA
RX FIFO, its COUNT register holds the filled bytes and the samples are
read from the 8-word port at +0x3000, by the same hrtimer. Capture takes
1-8 consecutive slots from rx_slot_base (default 4).

DAI 0 stays the playback-only speaker DAI. DAI 1 has playback and
capture for the headset codec on the same bus; both playback DAIs feed
the one TX slot, so the second playback open gets -EBUSY. The MCA reset
in hw_init now only runs when no other stream is prepared.

With #clock-cells the node also registers the MCLK pads of MCA0-4
(nclk / 2 = 12 MHz) as gate clocks.

The RX control word as clock master is a guess (0x20a, by analogy with
TX 0x208 vs the iOS slave value 0x108); the speaker path keeps writing
the iOS values.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
